  "aiSummary": "This is a Senate confirmation resolution that approves Nathaniel Denny's appointment as Secretary of the North Carolina Department of Information Technology. The resolution was adopted by the Senate on May 13, 2026, and becomes effective immediately.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters of this confirmation believe Nathaniel Denny is qualified to lead the state's IT department and manage information technology operations for North Carolina state government. Confirming experienced leadership for this role ensures continuity and effectiveness in managing the state's critical technology infrastructure and services.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may argue concerns about Denny's qualifications, experience, or previous record in IT management, or may question whether sufficient vetting occurred during the confirmation process. Some might also express broader concerns about the department's direction or budget priorities under new leadership.",
